# Settings that must not be committed. Copy this file and fill it in:
#
#     cp .env.example .env
#
# .env is git-ignored. Nothing here is required — with no topic set, a run sends no
# notifications and behaves exactly the same otherwise.

# The ntfy topic a run pushes to, so a long SLURM job need not be watched: one
# notification when a phase starts, one when it finishes, and one when the run ends,
# saying whether it succeeded or failed. Subscribe to the same topic in the ntfy phone or
# web app. docs/HPC/RUNNING.md describes the messages.
#
# ntfy has no accounts or passwords: anyone who knows the topic can read every message
# and post to it, and the messages carry the run name and launch directory. The name is
# the password, which is why the real one is not in this file. Ask whoever set up the
# project's topic, or run `uuidgen` for your own.
NTFY_TOPIC=

# A self-hosted ntfy instead of the public ntfy.sh. Optional.
# NTFY_SERVER=https://ntfy.example.org
